use /lib/UiComponent

export ui-component Rating:
    description:
        A rating shows a score on a small scale as a row of symbols, usually
        five stars. It can let the user give a score, or just show one.

    scale:
        The number of symbols is fixed, usually five. A score can be whole
        symbols only, or allow halves or smaller parts.

    interactive:
        The user clicks a symbol to give that score. Hovering previews the
        score before clicking. From the keyboard it is one stop in the Tab
        order, and the arrow keys raise and lower the score by one step.

    noScore:
        Having no score is different from a score of zero. The component
        decides whether the user can clear their score; if they can, clicking
        the current score again clears it.

    readOnly:
        A read-only rating just shows a score, such as an average of 4.3. It
        can show part of a symbol filled. Assistive tools read it out as text,
        such as "4.3 out of 5".

    name:
        A rating has a name saying what is being rated.
